  {
    "section": "genetics",
    "html": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\" data-figure=\"10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 230\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig10-title fig10-desc\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:680px;height:auto;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif\"><title id=\"fig10-title\">Direct expression reporter versus recombination memory</title><desc id=\"fig10-desc\">A direct reporter may fade after gene X turns off. A recombined permanent reporter continues to mark descendants if its promoter remains active.</desc><defs><marker id=\"arrow10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"var(--ink)\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"120\" y=\"18\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Early X positive</text><text x=\"403\" y=\"18\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Later X negative</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"40\" width=\"180\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"#76bc9a\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"67.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Direct reporter ON</text><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"302\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow10)\"/><rect x=\"310\" y=\"40\" width=\"180\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"67.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Reporter OFF</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"132\" width=\"180\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"#76bc9a\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"159.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Cre removes STOP</text><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"302\" y2=\"154\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow10)\"/><rect x=\"310\" y=\"132\" width=\"180\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"#76bc9a\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"159.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Reporter remains ON</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"212\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Permanent DNA change is inherited</text> </svg><figcaption>Figure 10. Direct expression reporter versus recombination memory. A direct reporter may fade after gene X turns off. A recombined permanent reporter continues to mark descendants if its promoter remains active.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn figure-zoom\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"
  },
  {
    "section": "experiments",
    "html": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\" data-figure=\"11\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 255\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig11-title fig11-desc\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:680px;height:auto;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif\"><title id=\"fig11-title\">Tracing, isolation and transplantation ask different questions</title><desc id=\"fig11-desc\">The same origin can be tracked without manipulation, isolated into a permissive setting or relocated into an alternative tissue. Interpret the endpoints relative to the conditions.</desc><defs><marker id=\"arrow11\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"var(--ink)\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"125\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#d8a342\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"130\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >A</text><line x1=\"105\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"285\" y2=\"46\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow11)\"/><line x1=\"105\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"285\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow11)\"/><line x1=\"105\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"285\" y2=\"204\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow11)\"/><rect x=\"295\" y=\"24\" width=\"205\" height=\"43\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"397.5\" y=\"50.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Normal fate</text><rect x=\"295\" y=\"103\" width=\"205\" height=\"43\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"397.5\" y=\"129.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Specification test</text><rect x=\"295\" y=\"182\" width=\"205\" height=\"43\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"397.5\" y=\"208.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Determination test</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"170\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Source cell</text> </svg><figcaption>Figure 11. Tracing, isolation and transplantation ask different questions. The same origin can be tracked without manipulation, isolated into a permissive setting or relocated into an alternative tissue. Interpret the endpoints relative to the conditions.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn figure-zoom\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"
  },
  {
    "section": "interpretation",
    "html": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\" data-figure=\"12\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 260\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig12-title fig12-desc\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:680px;height:auto;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif\"><title id=\"fig12-title\">Graft responsiveness at two donor ages</title><desc id=\"fig12-desc\">Hypothetical data: 30 of 40 viable early grafts and 8 of 40 viable late grafts adopt the alternative fate, with host stage held constant.</desc><defs><marker id=\"arrow12\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"var(--ink)\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"208\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"208\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"208\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><text x=\"45\" y=\"212\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >0%</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"208\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"208\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><text x=\"45\" y=\"170.75\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >25%</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"166.75\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"166.75\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><text x=\"45\" y=\"129.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >50%</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"125.5\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"125.5\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><text x=\"45\" y=\"88.25\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >75%</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"84.25\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"84.25\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><text x=\"45\" y=\"47\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >100%</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"43\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"43\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><rect x=\"150\" y=\"84.25\" width=\"100\" height=\"123.75\" fill=\"#75b4e5\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\"/><rect x=\"330\" y=\"175\" width=\"100\" height=\"33\" fill=\"#d8a342\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"75\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >75%</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"167\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >20%</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"232\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Early donor</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"232\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Late donor</text> </svg><figcaption>Figure 12. Graft responsiveness at two donor ages. Hypothetical data: 30 of 40 viable early grafts and 8 of 40 viable late grafts adopt the alternative fate, with host stage held constant.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn figure-zoom\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"
  },
  {
    "section": "synthesis",
    "html": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\" data-figure=\"13\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 255\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig13-title fig13-desc\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:680px;height:auto;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif\"><title id=\"fig13-title\">Concept map of developmental evidence</title><desc id=\"fig13-desc\">Cell origin is linked to normal fate by tracing; perturbation tests capacity and causality. Movement, division, survival and differentiation contribute to the final tissue.</desc><defs><marker id=\"arrow13\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"var(--ink)\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"150\" y=\"12\" width=\"220\" height=\"43\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"38.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Identifiable source cell</text><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"77\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow13)\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"83\" width=\"220\" height=\"43\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"109.5\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Trace descendants</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"157\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow13)\"/><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"157\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow13)\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"163\" width=\"220\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"189\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Normal fate / ancestry</text><rect x=\"285\" y=\"163\" width=\"220\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"395\" y=\"189\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Perturbed outcome</text><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"205\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow13)\"/><line x1=\"395\" y1=\"205\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"var(--ink)\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow13)\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"246\" fill=\"var(--ink)\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" >Compare to infer mechanism</text> </svg><figcaption>Figure 13. Concept map of developmental evidence. Cell origin is linked to normal fate by tracing; perturbation tests capacity and causality. Movement, division, survival and differentiation contribute to the final tissue.</figcaption><button type=\"button\" class=\"tool-btn figure-zoom\">Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"
  }
]